107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Builders on Portaldot spend their first weeks on infrastructure that has nothing to do with their product. Each team writes its own scraper, stores events in its own schema, decodes contract logs by hand, and quietly accepts gaps when the connection drops. The work is duplicated across every project, the data is inconsistent between them, and the missing ranges are invisible to the people relying on it. That slows every launch and makes the ecosystem look thinner than it is.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
